summary:
- topic: Board Welcome and Upcoming Events
  text: The Board welcomed new member Eleni Richardson and announced the next regular
    board meeting on June 9th. The community was reminded about the school budget
    referendum on June 10th, with voting at the community center.
- topic: Superintendent's Report and Teacher Resignations
  text: Superintendent Angela Atkinson Duina acknowledged student representative Eliot
    Wertheimer's upcoming recognition. She reported on three teacher resignations
    from Kaler and Small Schools, clarifying that these were not directly related
    to budget cuts or reductions in force.
- topic: School Budget Referendum Information
  text: Superintendent Angela Atkinson Duina provided details on accessing information
    about the school budget referendum via tinyurl.com/schools26. This resource includes
    a budget summary, key facts, and the budget warrant.
- topic: Personnel Elections and New Job Description
  text: The Board approved the elections of Megan Brand as Art Teacher at SPHS and
    Alexandra Schlechty as School Counselor at Brown School. A new part-time Confidential
    Human Resources Assistant job description was also approved, which is part of
    a district office reorganization aimed at reducing total salaries.
- topic: Discussion on Personnel Matters
  text: Board members discussed the teacher resignations, with clarification from
    the Superintendent that these were not due to budget cuts affecting their specific
    roles. The nature of the 'confidential' Human Resources Assistant role was also
    clarified to the public.
- topic: Executive Session
  text: The Board voted unanimously to enter into executive session to discuss a confidential
    personnel matter, as permitted by MRSA§405(6)(A).
